From: Lars Grahmann <lars.grahmann@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:01:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/33] Record the crossverify result and the umockdev filter
 in the notes (not for upstream)

---
 PROTOCOL.md | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/PROTOCOL.md b/PROTOCOL.md
index fb3feebd..fa3141c6 100644
--- a/PROTOCOL.md
+++ b/PROTOCOL.md
@@ -463,6 +463,17 @@ Other findings from the traces and logs:
 - Open sequence: version, pairing and TLS only, see above.
 - The a1 object data read works, so list returns real prints.
 
+Crossverify after the umockdev recording (umockdev/20261029-*-crossverify.log):
+a temporary right middle print, verified 8 times with the left index, all no
+match, and 2 times with the right middle, both match. With the 5 identifies of
+the crossmatch run that is 13 wrong-finger attempts without a false accept, so
+the one verify match in session 1 is put down to the wrong finger with data
+behind it now.
+
+The umockdev recording replays offline. The FIDO interface of the key had to
+be filtered out of the capture (endpoints 0x01 and 0x81), the kernel's usbhid
+polls it and replay waits on those urbs otherwise.
+
